W-4: the -wsiblit flag -- the tiling A/B lever rides argv.

The shell (ut) has no env machinery at v1.0 (no export, no VAR= prefix,
and the env coreutil cannot set-and-run), so THY_WSI_BLIT cannot reach
the game from the harness as an environment variable. The mesa WSI
reads it with getenv at instance creation IN THIS PROCESS, so an
in-process setenv before Vulkan init is sufficient: -wsiblit on the
command line selects the BUFFER_BLIT swapchain arm (OPTIMAL-tiled
images + a per-present resolve-blit into the linear presentable);
default stays the LINEAR arm. One binary carries both legs of the
ratified comparison.

--- a/Quake/main_sdl.c	2026-08-31 20:57:44
+++ b/Quake/main_sdl.c	2026-08-31 20:57:53
@@ -82,6 +82,18 @@
 	host_parms = &parms;
 	parms.basedir = ".";
 
+	/* THYLACINE port (0005): the W-4 tiling A/B lever. The shell has no
+	 * env machinery at v1.0, so the flag rides argv: -wsiblit sets the
+	 * env var the mesa WSI reads at instance creation (same process, so
+	 * an in-process setenv is all it takes -- it just has to happen
+	 * before Vulkan init). Selects the BUFFER_BLIT swapchain arm
+	 * (tiled images + resolve-blit); default stays LINEAR. */
+	for (t = 1; t < argc; t++)
+	{
+		if (argv[t] && !strcmp(argv[t], "-wsiblit"))
+			setenv("THY_WSI_BLIT", "1", 1);
+	}
+
 	parms.argc = argc;
 	parms.argv = argv;
 
